(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[7] = [{"v":1,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"मय्यासक्तमनाः पार्थ योगं युञ्जन्मदाश्रयः ।\nअसंशयं समग्रं मां यथा ज्ञास्यसि तच्छृणु ॥","iast":"mayyāsaktamanāḥ pārtha yogaṃ yuñjanmadāśrayaḥ |\nasaṃśayaṃ samagraṃ māṃ yathā jñāsyasi tacchṛṇu ||","read":"mayyaasaktamanaah paartha yogam yunjanmadaashrayah |\nasamshayam samagram maam yathaa jnaasyasi tachchhrinu ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: With the mind clinging to me, O Pârtha, performing yoga, refuged in Me, how thou shalt without doubt know Me to the uttermost, that hear thou.","en2":"With the mind intent on Me, O son of Prithâ, taking refuge in Me, and practising Yoga, how thou shalt without doubt know Me fully, that do thou hear.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna to listen. With his mind fixed on Krishna, practising and taking shelter in him, Arjuna will come to know Krishna fully, without any doubt."},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ज्ञानं तेऽहं सविज्ञानमिदं वक्ष्याम्यशेषतः ।\nयज्ज्ञात्वा नेह भूयोऽन्यज्ज्ञातव्यमवशिष्यते ॥","iast":"jñānaṃ te’haṃ savijñānamidaṃ vakṣyāmyaśeṣataḥ |\nyajjñātvā neha bhūyo’nyajjñātavyamavaśiṣyate ||","read":"jnaanam te'ham savijnaanamidam vakshyaamyasheshatah |\nyajjnaatvaa neha bhooyo'nyajjnaatavyamavashishyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I will declare to thee this knowledge and wisdom in its completeness, which, having known, there is nothing more here needeth to be known.","en2":"I shall tell you in full, of knowledge, speculative and practical, knowing which, nothing more here remains to be known.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he will explain this knowledge and wisdom completely. Once it is known, nothing more is left to know here."},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मनुष्याणां सहस्रेषु कश्चिद्यतति सिद्धये ।\nयततामपि सिद्धानां कश्चिन्मां वेत्ति तत्त्वतः ॥","iast":"manuṣyāṇāṃ sahasreṣu kaścidyatati siddhaye |\nyatatāmapi siddhānāṃ kaścinmāṃ vetti tattvataḥ ||","read":"manushyaanaam sahasreshu kashchidyatati siddhaye |\nyatataamapi siddhaanaam kashchinmaam vetti tattvatah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Among thousands of men scarce one striveth for perfection; of the successful strivers scarce one knoweth Me in essence.","en2":"One, perchance, in thousands of men, strives for perfection; and one perchance, among the blessed ones, striving thus, knows Me in reality.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that among thousands of people, hardly one tries for perfection. And among those who try, hardly one truly knows him."},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"भूमिरापोऽनलो वायुः खं मनो बुद्धिरेव च ।\nअहङ्कार इतीयं मे भिन्ना प्रकृतिरष्टधा ॥","iast":"bhūmirāpo’nalo vāyuḥ khaṃ mano buddhireva ca |\nahaṅkāra itīyaṃ me bhinnā prakṛtiraṣṭadhā ||","read":"bhoomiraapo'nalo vaayuh kham mano buddhireva cha |\nahankaara iteeyam me bhinnaa prakritirashtadhaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Earth, water, fire, air, ether, Mind, and Reason also and Egoism—these are the eightfold division of My nature.","en2":"Bhumi (earth), Ap (water), Anala (fire), Vâyu (air), Kha (ether), mind, intellect, and egoism: thus is My Prakriti divided eight-fold.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that his nature is divided into eight parts: earth, water, fire, air, space, mind, reason and ego."},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अपरेयमितस्त्वन्यां प्रकृतिं विद्धि मे पराम् ।\nजीवभूतां महाबाहो ययेदं धार्यते जगत् ॥","iast":"apareyamitastvanyāṃ prakṛtiṃ viddhi me parām |\njīvabhūtāṃ mahābāho yayedaṃ dhāryate jagat ||","read":"apareyamitastvanyaam prakritim viddhi me paraam |\njeevabhootaam mahaabaaho yayedam dhaaryate jagat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"This the inferior. Know My other nature, the higher, the life-element, O mighty-armed, by which the universe is upheld.","en2":"This is the lower (Prakriti). But different from it, know thou, O mighty-armed, My higher Prakriti—the principle of self-consciousness, by which this universe is sustained.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that this is his lower nature. He also has another, higher nature, and it is what holds up the whole universe."},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एतद्योनीनि भूतानि सर्वाणीत्युपधारय ।\nअहं कृत्स्नस्य जगतः प्रभवः प्रलयस्तथा ॥","iast":"etadyonīni bhūtāni sarvāṇītyupadhāraya |\nahaṃ kṛtsnasya jagataḥ prabhavaḥ pralayastathā ||","read":"etadyoneeni bhootaani sarvaaneetyupadhaaraya |\naham kritsnasya jagatah prabhavah pralayastathaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Know this to be the womb of all beings. I am the source of the forthgoing of the whole universe and likewise the place of its dissolving.","en2":"Know that these (two Prakritis) are the womb of all beings. I am the origin and dissolution of the whole universe.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says these are the womb from which all beings come. He is where the whole universe comes from, and where it dissolves again."},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मत्तः परतरं नान्यत्किञ्चिदस्ति धनञ्जय ।\nमयि सर्वमिदं प्रोतं सूत्रे मणिगणा इव ॥","iast":"mattaḥ parataraṃ nānyatkiñcidasti dhanañjaya |\nmayi sarvamidaṃ protaṃ sūtre maṇigaṇā iva ||","read":"mattah parataram naanyatkinchidasti dhananjaya |\nmayi sarvamidam protam sootre maniganaa iva ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"There is naught whatsoever higher than I, O Dhananjaya. All this is threaded on Me, as rows of pearls on a string.","en2":"Beyond Me, O Dhananjaya, there is naught. All this is strung in Me, as a row of jewels on a thread.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that there is nothing higher than him. Everything is strung on him, like a row of jewels on a string."},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"रसोऽहमप्सु कौन्तेय प्रभास्मि शशिसूर्ययोः ।\nप्रणवः सर्ववेदेषु शब्दः खे पौरुषं नृषु ॥","iast":"raso’hamapsu kaunteya prabhāsmi śaśisūryayoḥ |\npraṇavaḥ sarvavedeṣu śabdaḥ khe pauruṣaṃ nṛṣu ||","read":"raso'hamapsu kaunteya prabhaasmi shashisooryayoh |\npranavah sarvavedeshu shabdah khe paurusham nrishu ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I the sapidity in waters, O son of Kuntî, I the radiance in moon and sun; the Word of Power in all the Vedas, sound in ether, and virility in men;","en2":"I am the sapidity in waters, O son of Kunti; I, the radiance in the moon and the sun; I am the Om in all the Vedas, sound in Akâsha, and manhood in men.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he is the taste in water, the light in the moon and sun, the Word of Power in all the Vedas, the sound in space, and the manhood in men."},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"पुण्यो गन्धः पृथिव्यां च तेजश्चास्मि विभावसौ ।\nजीवनं सर्वभूतेषु तपश्चास्मि तपस्विषु ॥","iast":"puṇyo gandhaḥ pṛthivyāṃ ca tejaścāsmi vibhāvasau |\njīvanaṃ sarvabhūteṣu tapaścāsmi tapasviṣu ||","read":"punyo gandhah prithivyaam cha tejashchaasmi vibhaavasau |\njeevanam sarvabhooteshu tapashchaasmi tapasvishu ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The pure fragrance of earths and the bril liance in fire am I; the life in all beings am I, and the austerity in ascetics.","en2":"I am the sweet fragrance in earth, and the brilliance in fire am I; the life in all beings, and the austerity am I in ascetics.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he is the sweet smell of the earth and the brightness in fire. He is the life in all beings, and the self-discipline of those who live hard, simple lives."},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बीजं मां सर्वभूतानां विद्धि पार्थ सनातनम् ।\nबुद्धिर्बुद्धिमतामस्मि तेजस्तेजस्विनामहम् ॥","iast":"bījaṃ māṃ sarvabhūtānāṃ viddhi pārtha sanātanam |\nbuddhirbuddhimatāmasmi tejastejasvināmaham ||","read":"beejam maam sarvabhootaanaam viddhi paartha sanaatanam |\nbuddhirbuddhimataamasmi tejastejasvinaamaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Know Me, O Pârtha! as the eternal seed of all beings. I am the Reason of the Reason-endowed, the splendour of splendid things am I.","en2":"Know Me, O son of Prithâ, as the eternal seed of all beings. I am the intellect of the intelligent, and the heroism of the heroic.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells the son of Pritha to know him as the eternal seed of all beings. He says he is the intellect of the intelligent, and the splendor or heroism of the heroic."},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बलं बलवतां चाहं कामरागविवर्जितम् ।\nधर्माविरुद्धो भूतेषु कामोऽस्मि भरतर्षभ ॥","iast":"balaṃ balavatāṃ cāhaṃ kāmarāgavivarjitam |\ndharmāviruddho bhūteṣu kāmo’smi bharatarṣabha ||","read":"balam balavataam chaaham kaamaraagavivarjitam |\ndharmaaviruddho bhooteshu kaamo'smi bharatarshabha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And I the strength of the strong, devoid of desire and passion. In beings I am desire not contrary to duty, O Lord of the Bharatas.","en2":"Of the strong, I am the strength devoid of desire and attachment. I am, O bull among the Bhâratas, desire in beings, unopposed to Dharma.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he is the strength of the strong, free from desire and attachment. In all beings, he is the desire that does not go against what is right."},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ये चैव सात्त्विका भावा राजसास्तामसाश्च ये ।\nमत्त एवेति तान्विद्धि नत्वहं तेषु ते मयि ॥","iast":"ye caiva sāttvikā bhāvā rājasāstāmasāśca ye |\nmatta eveti tānviddhi natvahaṃ teṣu te mayi ||","read":"ye chaiva saattvikaa bhaavaa raajasaastaamasaashcha ye |\nmatta eveti taanviddhi natvaham teshu te mayi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The natures that are harmonious, active, slothful, these know as from Me; not I in them, but they in me.","en2":"And whatever states pertaining to Sattva, and those pertaining to Rajas, and to Tamas, know them to proceed from Me alone; still I am not in them, but they are in Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that all states of being, whether harmonious, active or lazy, come from him. He is not in them, but they are in him."},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"त्रिभिर्गुणमयैर्भावैरेभिः सर्वमिदं जगत् ।\nमोहितं नाभिजानाति मामेभ्यः परमव्ययम् ॥","iast":"tribhirguṇamayairbhāvairebhiḥ sarvamidaṃ jagat |\nmohitaṃ nābhijānāti māmebhyaḥ paramavyayam ||","read":"tribhirgunamayairbhaavairebhih sarvamidam jagat |\nmohitam naabhijaanaati maamebhyah paramavyayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"All this world, deluded by these natures made by the three qualities, knoweth not Me, above these, imperishable.","en2":"Deluded by these states, the modifications of the three Gunas (of Prakriti), all this world does not know Me, beyond them, and immutable.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the whole world is fooled by these states made of the three qualities. So it does not know him, who is above them and lasts for ever."},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"दैवी ह्येषा गुणमयी मम माया दुरत्यया ।\nमामेव ये प्रपद्यन्ते मायामेतां तरन्ति ते ॥","iast":"daivī hyeṣā guṇamayī mama māyā duratyayā |\nmāmeva ye prapadyante māyāmetāṃ taranti te ||","read":"daivee hyeshaa gunamayee mama maayaa duratyayaa |\nmaameva ye prapadyante maayaametaam taranti te ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"This divine illusion of Mine, caused by the qualities, is hard to pierce; they who come to Me, they cross over this illusion.","en2":"Verily, this divine illusion of Mine, constituted of the Gunas, is difficult to cross over; those who devote themselves to Me alone, cross over this illusion.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says this divine illusion of his, made of the qualities, is hard to get past. But those who come to him cross over it."},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न मां दुष्कृतिनो मूढाः प्रपद्यन्ते नराधमाः ।\nमाययापहृतज्ञाना आसुरं भावमाश्रिताः ॥","iast":"na māṃ duṣkṛtino mūḍhāḥ prapadyante narādhamāḥ |\nmāyayāpahṛtajñānā āsuraṃ bhāvamāśritāḥ ||","read":"na maam dushkritino moodhaah prapadyante naraadhamaah |\nmaayayaapahritajnaanaa aasuram bhaavamaashritaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The evil-doing, the deluded, the vilest men, they come not to Me, they whose wisdom is destroyed by illusion, who have embraced the nature of demons.","en2":"They do not devote themselves to Me,—the evil-doers, the deluded, the lowest of men, deprived of discrimination by Mâyâ, and following the way of the Asuras.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that people who do evil, who are fooled, and who are the lowest of people do not turn to him. Illusion has taken away their wisdom, and they follow the ways of demons."},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"चतुर्विधा भजन्ते मां जनाः सुकृतिनोऽर्जुन ।\nआर्तो जिज्ञासुरर्थार्थी ज्ञानी च भरतर्षभ ॥","iast":"caturvidhā bhajante māṃ janāḥ sukṛtino’rjuna |\nārto jijñāsurarthārthī jñānī ca bharatarṣabha ||","read":"chaturvidhaa bhajante maam janaah sukritino'rjuna |\naarto jijnaasurarthaarthee jnaanee cha bharatarshabha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Fourfold in division are the righteous ones who worship me, O Arjuna; the suffering, the seeker for knowledge, the self-interested and the wise, O Lord of the Bhâratas.","en2":"Four kinds of virtuous men worship Me, O Arjuna,—the distressed, the seeker of knowledge, the seeker of enjoyment, and the wise, O bull among the Bhâratas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that four kinds of good people worship him: those who are suffering, those who seek knowledge, those who seek good things for themselves, and the wise."},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तेषां ज्ञानी नित्ययुक्त एकभक्तिर्विशिष्यते ।\nप्रियो हि ज्ञानिनोऽत्यर्थमहं स च मम प्रियः ॥","iast":"teṣāṃ jñānī nityayukta ekabhaktirviśiṣyate |\npriyo hi jñānino’tyarthamahaṃ sa ca mama priyaḥ ||","read":"teshaam jnaanee nityayukta ekabhaktirvishishyate |\npriyo hi jnaanino'tyarthamaham sa cha mama priyah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of these the wise, constantly harmonised, worshipping the One, is the best; I am supremely dear to the wise, and he is dear to Me.","en2":"Of them, the wise man, ever-steadfast, (and fired) with devotion to the One, excels; for supremely dear am I to the wise, and he is dear to Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that of these, the wise person is the best, always steady and devoted to the One. Krishna is very dear to the wise, and the wise one is dear to him."},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"उदाराः सर्व एवैते ज्ञानी त्वात्मैव मे मतम् ।\nआस्थितः स हि युक्तात्मा मामेवानुत्तमां गतिम् ॥","iast":"udārāḥ sarva evaite jñānī tvātmaiva me matam |\nāsthitaḥ sa hi yuktātmā māmevānuttamāṃ gatim ||","read":"udaaraah sarva evaite jnaanee tvaatmaiva me matam |\naasthitah sa hi yuktaatmaa maamevaanuttamaam gatim ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Noble are all these, but I hold the wise as verily Myself; he, Self united, is fixed on Me, the highest Path.","en2":"Noble indeed are they all, but the wise man I regard as My very Self; for with the mind steadfast, he is established in Me alone, as the supreme goal.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says all of them are noble, but he sees the wise person as his very own Self. With a steady mind, the wise one is fixed on Krishna as the highest goal."},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बहूनां जन्मनामन्ते ज्ञानवान्मां प्रपद्यते ।\nवासुदेवः सर्वमिति स महात्मा सुदुर्लभः ॥","iast":"bahūnāṃ janmanāmante jñānavānmāṃ prapadyate |\nvāsudevaḥ sarvamiti sa mahātmā sudurlabhaḥ ||","read":"bahoonaam janmanaamante jnaanavaanmaam prapadyate |\nvaasudevah sarvamiti sa mahaatmaa sudurlabhah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"At the close of many births the man full of wisdom cometh unto Me; \"Vâsudeva is all.\" saith he, the Mahâtmâ, very difficult to find.","en2":"At the end of many births, the man of wisdom takes refuge in Me, realising that all this is Vâsudeva (the innermost Self). Very rare is that great soul.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that at the end of many births, the wise person comes to him, knowing that he is all. Such a great soul is very hard to find."},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कामैस्तैस्तैर्हृतज्ञानाः प्रपद्यन्तेऽन्यदेवताः ।\nतं तं नियममास्थाय प्रकृत्या नियताः स्वया ॥","iast":"kāmaistaistairhṛtajñānāḥ prapadyante’nyadevatāḥ |\ntaṃ taṃ niyamamāsthāya prakṛtyā niyatāḥ svayā ||","read":"kaamaistaistairhritajnaanaah prapadyante'nyadevataah |\ntam tam niyamamaasthaaya prakrityaa niyataah svayaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They whose wisdom hath been rent away by desires go forth to other Shining Ones, resorting to various external observances, according to their own natures.","en2":"Others again, deprived of discrimination by this or that desire, following this or that rite, devote themselves to other gods, led by their own natures.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that people whose wisdom has been carried off by desires turn to other Shining Ones. They follow different practices, each led by their own nature."},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यो यो यां यां तनुं भक्तः श्रद्धयार्चितुमिच्छति ।\nतस्य तस्याचलां श्रद्धां तामेव विदधाम्यहम् ॥","iast":"yo yo yāṃ yāṃ tanuṃ bhaktaḥ śraddhayārcitumicchati |\ntasya tasyācalāṃ śraddhāṃ tāmeva vidadhāmyaham ||","read":"yo yo yaam yaam tanum bhaktah shraddhayaarchitumichchhati |\ntasya tasyaachalaam shraddhaam taameva vidadhaamyaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Any devotee who seeketh to worship with faith any such aspect, I verily bestow the unswerving faith of that man.","en2":"Whatsoever form any devotee seeks to worship with Shraddhâ,—that Shraddhâ of his do I make unwavering.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that whatever form a devotee wants to worship with faith, Krishna makes that person's faith firm and steady."},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"स तया श्रद्धया युक्तस्तस्याराधनमीहते ।\nलभते च ततः कामान्मयैव विहितान् हि तान् ॥","iast":"sa tayā śraddhayā yuktastasyārādhanamīhate |\nlabhate ca tataḥ kāmānmayaiva vihitān hi tān ||","read":"sa tayaa shraddhayaa yuktastasyaaraadhanameehate |\nlabhate cha tatah kaamaanmayaiva vihitaan hi taan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He endowed with that faith, seeketh the worship of such a one, and from him he obtaineth his desires, I verily decreeing the benefits;","en2":"Endued with that Shraddhâ, he engages in the worship of that, and from it, gains his desires,—these being verily dispensed by Me alone.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that with that faith, the person worships that form and gets what he wishes for. But it is really Krishna who gives these gifts."},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अन्तवत्तु फलं तेषां तद्भवत्यल्पमेधसाम् ।\nदेवान्देवयजो यान्ति मद्भक्ता यान्ति मामपि ॥","iast":"antavattu phalaṃ teṣāṃ tadbhavatyalpamedhasām |\ndevāndevayajo yānti madbhaktā yānti māmapi ||","read":"antavattu phalam teshaam tadbhavatyalpamedhasaam |\ndevaandevayajo yaanti madbhaktaa yaanti maamapi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Finite indeed the fruit that belongeth to those who are of small intelligence. To the Shining Ones go the worshippers of the Shining Ones, but my devotees come unto Me.","en2":"But the fruit (accruing) to these men of little understanding is limited. The worshippers of the Devas go to the Devas; My devotees too come to me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that the reward for those with little understanding has a limit. Those who worship the Shining Ones go to the Shining Ones, and those devoted to Krishna come to him."},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अव्यक्तं व्यक्तिमापन्नं मन्यन्ते मामबुद्धयः ।\nपरं भावमजानन्तो ममाव्ययमनुत्तमम् ॥","iast":"avyaktaṃ vyaktimāpannaṃ manyante māmabuddhayaḥ |\nparaṃ bhāvamajānanto mamāvyayamanuttamam ||","read":"avyaktam vyaktimaapannam manyante maamabuddhayah |\nparam bhaavamajaananto mamaavyayamanuttamam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Those devoid of Reason think of Me, the unmanifest, as having manifestation, knowing not My supreme nature, imperishable, most excellent.","en2":"The foolish regard Me, the un-manifested, as come into manifestation, not knowing My supreme state,—immutable and transcendental.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that people without understanding think that he, who cannot be seen, has taken a form. They do not know his highest nature, which is beyond all and everlasting."},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नाहं प्रकाशः सर्वस्य योगमायासमावृतः ।\nमूढोऽयं नाभिजानाति लोको मामजमव्ययम् ॥","iast":"nāhaṃ prakāśaḥ sarvasya yogamāyāsamāvṛtaḥ |\nmūḍho’yaṃ nābhijānāti loko māmajamavyayam ||","read":"naaham prakaashah sarvasya yogamaayaasamaavritah |\nmoodho'yam naabhijaanaati loko maamajamavyayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor am I of all discovered, enveloped in My creation-illusion. This deluded world knoweth Me not, the unborn, the imperishable.","en2":"Veiled by the illusion born of the congress of the Gunas, I am not manifest to all. This deluded world knows Me not, the Unborn, the Immutable.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he is not seen by everyone, because he is covered by illusion. This confused world does not know him, the unborn one who lasts for ever."},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"वेदाहं समतीतानि वर्तमानानि चार्जुन ।\nभविष्याणि च भूतानि मां तु वेद न कश्चन ॥","iast":"vedāhaṃ samatītāni vartamānāni cārjuna |\nbhaviṣyāṇi ca bhūtāni māṃ tu veda na kaścana ||","read":"vedaaham samateetaani vartamaanaani chaarjuna |\nbhavishyaani cha bhootaani maam tu veda na kashchana ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I know the beings that are past, that are present, that are to come, O Arjuna, but no one knoweth Me.","en2":"I know, O Arjuna, the beings of the whole past, and the present, and the future, but Me none knoweth.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that he knows all beings of the past, the present and the future. But no one knows him."},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इच्छाद्वेषसमुत्थेन द्वन्द्वमोहेन भारत ।\nसर्वभूतानि संमोहं सर्गे यान्ति परन्तप ॥","iast":"icchādveṣasamutthena dvandvamohena bhārata |\nsarvabhūtāni saṃmohaṃ sarge yānti parantapa ||","read":"ichchhaadveshasamutthena dvandvamohena bhaarata |\nsarvabhootaani sammoham sarge yaanti parantapa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"By the delusion of the pairs of opposites, sprung from attraction and repulsion, O Bhârata, all beings walk this universe wholly deluded, O Parantapa.","en2":"By the delusion of the pairs of opposites, arising from desire and aversion, O descendant of Bharata, all beings fall into delusion at birth, O scorcher of foes.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that all beings are fooled by pairs of opposites, which come from liking and disliking. Because of this, all beings fall into confusion."},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"येषां त्वन्तगतं पापं जनानां पुण्यकर्मणाम् ।\nते द्वन्द्वमोहनिर्मुक्ता भजन्ते मां दृढव्रताः ॥","iast":"yeṣāṃ tvantagataṃ pāpaṃ janānāṃ puṇyakarmaṇām |\nte dvandvamohanirmuktā bhajante māṃ dṛḍhavratāḥ ||","read":"yeshaam tvantagatam paapam janaanaam punyakarmanaam |\nte dvandvamohanirmuktaa bhajante maam dridhavrataah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But those men of pure deeds, in whom sin is come to an end, they, freed from the delusive pairs of opposites, worship Me, steadfast in vows.","en2":"Those men of virtuous deeds, whose sin has come to an end,—they, freed from the delusion of the pairs of opposites, worship Me with firm resolve.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that people who do good deeds, whose wrongdoing has come to an end, are freed from the confusion of opposites. They worship him, firm in their purpose."},{"v":29,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"जरामरणमोक्षाय मामाश्रित्य यतन्ति ये ।\nते ब्रह्म तद्विदुः कृत्स्नमध्यात्मं कर्म चाखिलम् ॥","iast":"jarāmaraṇamokṣāya māmāśritya yatanti ye |\nte brahma tadviduḥ kṛtsnamadhyātmaṃ karma cākhilam ||","read":"jaraamaranamokshaaya maamaashritya yatanti ye |\nte brahma tadviduh kritsnamadhyaatmam karma chaakhilam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They who, refuged in Me, strive for liberation from birth and death, they know the Eternal, the whole Self -knowledge, and all action.","en2":"Those who strive for freedom from old age and death, taking refuge in Me, they know. Brahman, the whole of Adhyâtma, and Karma in its entirety.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that those who take shelter in him and strive to be free from death know the Eternal, all about the Self, and all about action."},{"v":30,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"साधिभूताधिदैवं मां साधियज्ञं च ये विदुः ।\nप्रयाणकालेऽपि च मां ते विदुर्युक्तचेतसः ॥","iast":"sādhibhūtādhidaivaṃ māṃ sādhiyajñaṃ ca ye viduḥ |\nprayāṇakāle’pi ca māṃ te viduryuktacetasaḥ ||","read":"saadhibhootaadhidaivam maam saadhiyajnam cha ye viduh |\nprayaanakaale'pi cha maam te viduryuktachetasah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They who know Me as the knowledge of the elements, as that of the Shining Ones, and as that of the Sacrifice, they harmonised in mind, know Me verily even in the time of forthgoing.","en2":"Those who know Me with the Adhibhuta, the Adhidaiva, and the Adhiyajna, (continue to) know Me even at the time of death, steadfast in mind.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that those who know him in the elements, in the Shining Ones and in sacrifice keep their minds steady, and know him even at the time of death."}];
